&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, India, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, Indian, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members globally and rapidly growing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3,000 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognised with Great Place to Work certification three years in a row, and among India’s Top 50 Best Workplaces in Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance in 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we&#39;re building the leading financial platform for small businesses. As we continue to grow across multiple markets, strong financial risk management is essential to helping us scale safely, responsibly and sustainably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our &lt;strong&gt;Director of Financial Risk&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll lead our global 2LOD Financial Risk team and shape how we identify, assess and oversee financial risks across the business. You&#39;ll own our financial risk framework while providing independent oversight, challenge and trusted advice to 1LOD teams across:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial Reporting &amp;amp; Control (statutory &amp;amp; regulatory accounting),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FP&amp;amp;A (management accounting &amp;amp; commercial finance),&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance Operations (including account operations, reconciliations, AP &amp;amp; AR, payroll)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treasury&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance Product (systems support for Finance).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate Development (for any CorDev working impacting FinRisk)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As well as the Regional Heads/Directors of Finance that coordinate these functions for their region (UK, EU, India).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible leadership role, and you’ll be at the forefront of scaling in new markets, working on new licences, and new products. We are looking for not just a deep subject matter expert, but a trusted leader to help us scale whilst managing our financial risks.&amp;nbsp; You will need to be a strong collaborator, as you&#39;ll work closely with a variety of stakeholders, from senior leadership and executives to auditors and banking partners, to ensure Tide remains financially resilient while continuing to innovate for our members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE DOING&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a global role in which you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Tide&#39;s Financial Risk Management Framework, ensuring it grows with the business as we expand into new markets, launch new products and operate under new licences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide independent oversight and challenge of 1LOD activities relating to financial risks, working mostly with Finance and Treasury. You need to be deeply familiar with how a global Treasury function works, to be able to identify and manage risks arising.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure alignment of financial risk governance across all regulated entities and jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance financial risk appetite metrics, limits, triggers, and escalation protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clear and independent reporting to Group and entity-level Risk &amp;amp; Compliance Committees and Boards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor capital adequacy, liquidity, concentration risks, and financial resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory engagements, audits, thematic reviews, and licence applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently oversee treasury and liquidity management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and challenge liquidity forecasting methodologies and stress assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain existing risk policies and frameworks, and develop new ones as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead financial risk assessments for new products, partnerships, and market launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other Risk &amp;amp; Compliance teams, various Finance teams, Legal and Internal Audit teams to ensure integrated risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present concise and insightful risk reporting to Risk &amp;amp; Compliance Committees, and lead on the Financial Risk Working Groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a high-performing and experienced global financial risk team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who combines deep technical expertise with excellent judgement and the ability to influence across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll likely have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading Financial Risk within fintech, payments, e-money, banking or another regulated financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a 2LOD leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of financial risk frameworks within payment institutions, e-money institutions or digital banking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise across treasury, liquidity, solvability, capital, solvency, statutory reporting and tax risk.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accounting expertise; ideally with an accounting qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple regulatory jurisdictions and engaging directly with regulators and auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to balance strong risk management with commercial ambition in a fast-moving business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the confidence to influence senior stakeholders and provide independent challenge when it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative leadership style, with experience building and developing high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most importantly, you&#39;ll enjoy working in a fast-paced environment, be comfortable navigating change, and care about helping Tide build a resilient business that continues to deliver for our members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Compensation -&amp;nbsp; competitive salary and share options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time Off – Generous annual leave on top of bank holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave – Paid maternity, paternity, and adoption leave to support your family journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical – Extended unpaid and paid leave options after completing milestone years with Tide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to salary sacrifice benefits – like Nursery (could save up to 47% on fees!) and Cycle to Work discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance – Comprehensive Private family insurance plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Accident Cover – Comprehensive accidental and life insurance protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellbeing – Access to therapy sessions, courses, meditations, and workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Planning – Build your retirement fund faster with Tide’s pension scheme on eligible earnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteering &amp;amp; Development Days – Paid days annually for volunteering or personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development – Annual budget for books, courses, coaching, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WOO (Work Outside the Office) – Work from abroad for up to 90 days annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Setup – Contribution towards setting up your home office&lt;/li&gt;
